    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d328">

                <pb facs="1224" n="1049" sameAs="frus:frus1961-63v10-12mSupp/pg1049"/>

                <head>328. Gilpatric’s handwritten notes of meeting, October 17<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d328-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <date ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-head" calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1962-10-17">October 17, 1962</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <pb facs="d328-1" n="1" type="facsimile" xml:id="d328-1"/>
                <p>Rusk</p>
                <p>10/17/62</p>
                <p>1) U.S. cannot accept MRBMs in Cuba</p>
                <p>2) no profit from preliminary exchange with K&amp;C</p>
                <p>3) hold until middle of next week</p>
                <p>4) then execute Plan I after informing key allies, U.K., France, Germany perhaps
                    Turkey, &amp; some LA nations (such as Venezuela) at same time notifying K, NAC,
                    OAS, &amp; UN</p>
                <p>5) be prepared for Soviet reactions in Turkey, Berlin, Korea, &amp; Taiwan
                    (Quemoy &amp; Matsu)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d328-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d328-f1-content">
                <p>U.S. position on missiles in Cuba. Top Secret. 1 p. WNRC, RG 330, OASD (C) A
                    Files: FRC 71 A 2896, RLG’s Notes re Cuba.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
